WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.095
Picture a salesperson in an underground

2
00:00:03.095 --> 00:00:05.675
parking garage, with no signal at all.

3
00:00:06.095 --> 00:00:07.481
This repository is

4
00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:09.145
built for that moment.

5
00:00:09.565 --> 00:00:11.804
It is Odoo 20, forked so the

6
00:00:11.804 --> 00:00:14.565
CRM pipeline keeps working offline.

7
00:00:14.985 --> 00:00:16.807
You can still save a lead,

8
00:00:16.807 --> 00:00:18.760
move a stage, or log a call.

9
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.200
Each write waits safely, then

10
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.480
replays when the network returns.

11
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.644
On screen is the desktop

12
00:00:25.644 --> 00:00:27.925
pipeline this work started from.

13
00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.525
First, the shape of the codebase.

14
00:00:31.945 --> 00:00:35.159
Upstream Odoo is one Python server

15
00:00:35.159 --> 00:00:38.195
surrounded by 642 addon modules.

16
00:00:38.615 --> 00:00:40.890
That adds up to about 1.36

17
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.653
million lines of Python and 1.51

18
00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:46.090
million lines of JavaScript.

19
00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.736
Its history starts in December

20
00:00:48.736 --> 00:00:50.545
2006, with more than two

21
00:00:50.545 --> 00:00:52.910
hundred eleven thousand commits.

22
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.730
The fork is small by comparison.

23
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.257
It adds seventy-six commits, from

24
00:00:59.257 --> 00:01:02.275
September 30 to October 5, 2026.

25
00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.808
Every product change lives

26
00:01:04.808 --> 00:01:06.770
inside addons slash crm.

27
00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.272
Next, how a request

28
00:01:09.272 --> 00:01:10.945
moves through the server.

29
00:01:11.365 --> 00:01:13.353
The odoo-bin command starts a

30
00:01:13.353 --> 00:01:15.790
threaded, prefork, or gevent server.

31
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.160
Each database gets its own

32
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.110
registry of loaded models.

33
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.559
The HTTP dispatcher routes

34
00:01:22.559 --> 00:01:24.805
each request to a controller.

35
00:01:25.225 --> 00:01:27.782
Controllers call the ORM, which

36
00:01:27.782 --> 00:01:30.650
batches its writes into PostgreSQL.

37
00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.720
The offline work never

38
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.095
changes this path.

39
00:01:34.515 --> 00:01:36.515
It only decides when a browser

40
00:01:36.515 --> 00:01:38.390
call is allowed to reach it.

41
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.063
The browser side is

42
00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:42.465
an OWL web client.

43
00:01:42.885 --> 00:01:45.003
It is layered from core plugins,

44
00:01:45.003 --> 00:01:46.935
up through views and actions.

45
00:01:47.355 --> 00:01:49.028
The key point is that the

46
00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:51.072
offline framework already lives

47
00:01:51.072 --> 00:01:53.055
here, inside addons slash web.

48
00:01:53.475 --> 00:01:54.967
It owns the sync queue,

49
00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:56.996
the encrypted store, the service

50
00:01:56.996 --> 00:01:59.025
worker, and the offline systray.

51
00:01:59.445 --> 00:02:02.395
The CRM fork consumes that framework.

52
00:02:02.815 --> 00:02:05.190
It never builds a second one.

53
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.953
Here is the lifecycle

54
00:02:07.953 --> 00:02:09.515
of one offline write.

55
00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:11.358
A save fails with a

56
00:02:11.358 --> 00:02:12.985
connection lost error.

57
00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:16.070
The offline plugin stores the exact

58
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.880
call in an encrypted IndexedDB table.

59
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.596
On reconnect, entries replay in

60
00:02:21.596 --> 00:02:24.100
timestamp order, one second apart.

61
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.458
Last write wins, and there

62
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:28.120
is no conflict dialog.

63
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.220
A call that fails for any

64
00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.086
other reason is parked under

65
00:02:32.086 --> 00:02:33.890
Sync issues in the systray.

66
00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.465
So which controls may queue at all?

67
00:02:37.885 --> 00:02:40.482
The fork answered that with an inventory,

68
00:02:40.482 --> 00:02:42.535
before writing any feature code.

69
00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:45.526
Every entry point in the CRM addon

70
00:02:45.526 --> 00:02:47.955
got exactly one of three labels.

71
00:02:48.375 --> 00:02:49.849
Queue means a write the

72
00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:51.500
client can fully describe.

73
00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.595
Skip means a decorative

74
00:02:53.595 --> 00:02:55.270
read, silently dropped.

75
00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.955
Disable covers everything else,

76
00:02:57.955 --> 00:03:00.015
such as wizards and reports.

77
00:03:00.435 --> 00:03:02.758
The final count is 150 rows,

78
00:03:02.758 --> 00:03:05.235
and most of them are disabled.

79
00:03:06.435 --> 00:03:09.060
Disabling is mostly automatic.

80
00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.817
The framework turns

81
00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:12.727
off every button without the

82
00:03:12.727 --> 00:03:14.955
data-available-offline attribute.

83
00:03:15.375 --> 00:03:18.248
But links, menu items, and already-open

84
00:03:18.248 --> 00:03:20.350
dialogs slip past that pass.

85
00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:22.447
Guard patches in the view

86
00:03:22.447 --> 00:03:24.745
components folder close those gaps.

87
00:03:25.165 --> 00:03:27.325
Each one re-checks the connection

88
00:03:27.325 --> 00:03:29.115
at the moment of the click.

89
00:03:29.535 --> 00:03:32.165
A view never visited online shows the

90
00:03:32.165 --> 00:03:34.660
framework's offline helper instead.

91
00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.933
Some writes needed a server change

92
00:03:37.933 --> 00:03:39.660
before they could be queued.

93
00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.639
The queue replays calls

94
00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:43.572
verbatim, and never passes an

95
00:03:43.572 --> 00:03:45.505
id from one call to the next.

96
00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.818
So logging a call became a

97
00:03:47.818 --> 00:03:50.050
single method, action log call.

98
00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.602
It creates the call activity and

99
00:03:52.602 --> 00:03:54.545
marks it done in one request.

100
00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:57.007
In the same spirit, an activity

101
00:03:57.007 --> 00:03:59.235
create override fills in the model

102
00:03:59.235 --> 00:04:01.215
id for queued lead activities.

103
00:04:02.415 --> 00:04:04.401
On the client, every CRM

104
00:04:04.401 --> 00:04:06.768
component reads offline state

105
00:04:06.768 --> 00:04:09.365
through one hook, useCrmOffline.

106
00:04:09.785 --> 00:04:11.735
It wraps the framework plugin,

107
00:04:11.735 --> 00:04:13.685
and keeps no state of its own.

108
00:04:14.105 --> 00:04:15.836
It can queue a call, or list

109
00:04:15.836 --> 00:04:17.855
what is still pending for a lead.

110
00:04:18.275 --> 00:04:19.857
The team switcher shows

111
00:04:19.857 --> 00:04:21.375
why that care matters.

112
00:04:21.795 --> 00:04:23.309
Its data comes from the

113
00:04:23.309 --> 00:04:25.006
disk cache, and falls back

114
00:04:25.006 --> 00:04:26.520
to All Teams on a miss.

115
00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.701
A rejected group check would

116
00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.520
poison its cache for good, so

117
00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.340
it is re-probed on reconnect.

118
00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.190
Now, the phone.

119
00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.783
On small screens, the pipeline

120
00:04:37.783 --> 00:04:39.685
shows one stage at a time.

121
00:04:40.105 --> 00:04:42.166
That branch is gated on the UI

122
00:04:42.166 --> 00:04:44.355
plugin's small-screen signal, so

123
00:04:44.355 --> 00:04:46.480
desktop rendering is unchanged.

124
00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.270
A sticky header shows the stage name,

125
00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.700
the lead count, and the revenue total.

126
00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.735
Previous and next buttons step between

127
00:04:54.735 --> 00:04:57.220
stages without a network round trip.

128
00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.162
Each card is a forty-four pixel touch

129
00:05:00.162 --> 00:05:02.490
target, with a pending sync badge.

130
00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.211
The plus button opens a

131
00:05:05.211 --> 00:05:06.915
quick create bottom sheet.

132
00:05:07.335 --> 00:05:09.635
It has exactly six fields, with a

133
00:05:09.635 --> 00:05:12.460
plain stage selector instead of a search.

134
00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.687
Saving issues one web

135
00:05:14.687 --> 00:05:16.730
save, online or offline.

136
00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.742
Offline, that same call

137
00:05:18.742 --> 00:05:20.525
simply lands in the queue.

138
00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:23.168
Until it replays, a pending card

139
00:05:23.168 --> 00:05:25.195
holds its place in the stage.

140
00:05:25.615 --> 00:05:28.036
When the queue drains, the real card

141
00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:30.265
replaces it, with no page reload.

142
00:05:31.465 --> 00:05:33.222
Installing the web app is

143
00:05:33.222 --> 00:05:35.240
the native mobile story here.

144
00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.610
There is no separate native app project.

145
00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.667
The CRM controller adds two manifest

146
00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:44.305
shortcuts, My Pipeline and New Lead.

147
00:05:44.725 --> 00:05:46.541
It also enables the share

148
00:05:46.541 --> 00:05:48.492
target, so a file shared on

149
00:05:48.492 --> 00:05:50.375
the phone can open in CRM.

150
00:05:50.795 --> 00:05:52.816
All of it runs through the one

151
00:05:52.816 --> 00:05:55.595
service worker that web already registers.

152
00:05:56.795 --> 00:05:58.697
Testing gets special care,

153
00:05:58.697 --> 00:06:00.395
because there is no CI.

154
00:06:00.815 --> 00:06:03.123
The raw test runner has three ways

155
00:06:03.123 --> 00:06:05.815
to report success while testing nothing.

156
00:06:06.235 --> 00:06:08.848
The dev scripts detect all three, and

157
00:06:08.848 --> 00:06:11.260
fail on skips or empty selections.

158
00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.762
Forty-six offline test files

159
00:06:13.762 --> 00:06:15.567
must pass under both the

160
00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.580
desktop and mobile presets.

161
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.546
An end-to-end tour then

162
00:06:19.546 --> 00:06:21.586
goes offline at phone size, and

163
00:06:21.586 --> 00:06:23.750
checks every write on the server.

164
00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.487
You can remember this

165
00:06:26.487 --> 00:06:28.425
repository as three layers.

166
00:06:28.845 --> 00:06:30.695
Upstream Odoo provides the

167
00:06:30.695 --> 00:06:32.545
server and the web client.

168
00:06:32.965 --> 00:06:35.815
The web addon owns the offline engine.

169
00:06:36.235 --> 00:06:38.338
The CRM fork decides, row by

170
00:06:38.338 --> 00:06:40.512
row, what queues, what skips,

171
00:06:40.512 --> 00:06:42.335
and what stays disabled.

172
00:06:42.755 --> 00:06:44.566
To start, read the inventory,

173
00:06:44.566 --> 00:06:46.144
then follow the hook, the

174
00:06:46.144 --> 00:06:48.130
guards, and the mobile pipeline.
